# Subagent models: Composer first, Grok for hard tasks

When delegating work to subagents (Task tool), pick the model explicitly:

## Composer (`composer-2.5-fast`) — default

Use for routine, well-scoped work:
- codebase search / explore, reading files, grep-style questions
- mechanical edits across files, renames, wiring CTAs, frontmatter, OG pins
- running scripts, publish commands, build/deploy checks, log reading
- small bug fixes where the cause is already known

## Grok (`grok-4.7-high-fast`) — complex tasks

Escalate to Grok when the task needs real reasoning:
- multi-step debugging with an unknown root cause
- architecture / pipeline design (Threads farm, satellites, parsers, LLM chains)
- fact-check of legal claims and thresholds (AIMA, BOE, IMT) against official sources
- long guide rewrites / editorial quality passes where tone and structure matter
- anything a Composer run already failed on

If `grok-4.7-high-fast` is unavailable, use `cursor-grok-4.6-high-fast`.

## Notes

- Do not silently substitute another model family; if neither Grok is available, say so.
- Content-generation scripts that call Grok via OpenRouter (`scripts/portugal-grok-rewrite-batch.ts`, model `x-ai/grok-4.3`) are separate from subagent choice — keep using them for guide rewrites.
